@startuml
title ThingsBoard 3.6 TimescaleDB telemetry: install, history/latest batches, chunk routing and TTL

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #253746
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #334155
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participantBorderColor #334155
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam participantFontColor #111827
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5CC
skinparam noteBorderColor #8A5A00
skinparam noteFontColor #111827
skinparam groupBorderColor #334155
skinparam groupHeaderBackgroundColor #E5E7EB
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam maxMessageSize 210

participant "Installer" as Installer
participant "Schema Service" as Schema
database "PostgreSQL" as PG
participant "Timescale Extension" as Timescale
participant "Rule Engine Queue" as Queue
participant "Save Timeseries Node" as Node
participant "Telemetry Service" as Telemetry
participant "BaseTimeseriesService" as Base
participant "Dictionary DAO" as Dictionary
participant "Timescale History DAO" as History
participant "History SQL Queue" as HistoryQueue
participant "History JDBC Repository" as HistoryRepo
participant "SQL Latest DAO" as Latest
participant "Latest SQL Queue" as LatestQueue
participant "Latest JDBC Repository" as LatestRepo
participant "Subscription Notify" as Notify
participant "TTL Scheduler" as TTL

== Install profile ==
Installer -> Schema : createDatabaseSchema()
Schema -> PG : CREATE EXTENSION timescaledb
Schema -> PG : CREATE ts_kv, dictionary, latest and cleanup procedure
Schema -> Timescale : create_hypertable(ts_kv, ts, chunk interval)
Timescale -> PG : register bigint time dimension and chunk metadata
PG --> Schema : success
note over Schema,Timescale
  Only ts_kv becomes a hypertable.
  Dictionary and latest remain ordinary PostgreSQL tables.
end note

== Telemetry entry ==
Queue -> Node : POST_TELEMETRY_REQUEST TbMsg
Node -> Node : parse entries, ttl and saveLatest
Node -> Telemetry : saveAndNotify(tenant, entity, entries, ttl, callback)
Telemetry -> Base : save(...) or saveWithoutLatest(...)

loop each TsKvEntry
  Base -> History : savePartition(entity, ts, key)
  History --> Base : immediateFuture(0)
  Base -> History : save(tenant, entity, entry, ttl)

  == Key dictionary ==
  History -> Dictionary : getOrSaveKeyId(string key)
  alt local ConcurrentMap hit
    Dictionary --> History : key_id
  else cache miss
    Dictionary -> PG : SELECT ts_kv_dictionary
    alt missing
      Dictionary -> Dictionary : acquire JVM creation lock
      Dictionary -> PG : INSERT key, generated key_id
      alt another service won unique race
        PG --> Dictionary : constraint violation
        Dictionary -> PG : SELECT existing key_id
      end
    end
    Dictionary --> History : key_id and cache
  end

  == History enqueue ==
  History -> History : build TimescaleTsKvEntity
  History -> HistoryQueue : add(entity), hash by entity UUID
  opt saveLatest
    Base -> Latest : saveLatest(entity, entry)
    Latest -> LatestQueue : add(TsKvLatestEntity)
  end
end

== Independent history batch transaction ==
HistoryQueue -> HistoryQueue : poll first, drain to batch size
HistoryQueue -> HistoryQueue : optionally sort entity_id, key, ts
HistoryQueue -> HistoryRepo : saveOrUpdate(batch)
HistoryRepo -> PG : JDBC batch INSERT ON CONFLICT
PG -> Timescale : route each logical ts_kv row by bigint ts
Timescale -> PG : write target internal chunk and indexes
alt history transaction commits
  PG --> HistoryRepo : update counts
  HistoryRepo --> HistoryQueue : return
  HistoryQueue --> Base : all batch Futures success
else SQL, lock, connection or chunk failure
  PG --> HistoryRepo : exception and rollback batch
  HistoryRepo --> HistoryQueue : throw
  HistoryQueue --> Base : all batch Futures failed
end

== Independent latest batch transaction ==
LatestQueue -> LatestQueue : poll and drain
LatestQueue -> LatestQueue : merge entity_id + key, retain max payload ts
LatestQueue -> LatestRepo : saveOrUpdate(trueLatest)
LatestRepo -> PG : UPDATE WHERE existing.ts <= incoming.ts
LatestRepo -> PG : INSERT ON CONFLICT for rows not updated
alt latest transaction commits
  PG --> LatestRepo : success
  LatestRepo --> LatestQueue : return
  LatestQueue --> Base : latest Futures success
else latest transaction fails
  PG --> LatestRepo : rollback and exception
  LatestQueue --> Base : latest Futures failed
end

== Combined application result ==
Base -> Base : Futures.allAsList(history and latest)
alt every registered Future succeeds
  Base --> Telemetry : success
  Telemetry -> Notify : publish telemetry update
  Telemetry --> Node : callback success
  Node --> Queue : Success relation
else any Future fails
  Base --> Telemetry : failed combination
  Telemetry --> Node : callback failure
  Node --> Queue : Failure relation
end
note over HistoryQueue,LatestQueue
  History and latest use different queues, connections and transactions.
  allAsList is not a database transaction and does not roll back partial commits.
end note

== Native query path ==
Node -> History : findAllAsync(entity, key, range, aggregation)
alt raw values
  History -> PG : SELECT ts range ORDER BY ts LIMIT
else fixed millisecond aggregation
  History -> PG : SELECT time_bucket(...) GROUP BY bucket
else calendar aggregation
  loop each calendar period
    History -> PG : one time_bucket query for period
  end
end
Timescale -> PG : planner excludes chunks outside ts range
PG --> History : rows or aggregate buckets

== ThingsBoard TTL path ==
TTL -> TTL : scheduled only on system tenant partition owner
TTL -> Base : cleanup(systemTtl)
Base -> History : cleanup(systemTtl)
History -> PG : CALL cleanup_timeseries_by_ttl
PG -> PG : read tenant/customer TTL attributes
PG -> PG : DELETE old device/asset/customer rows from ts_kv
PG --> History : deleted row count and warnings
note over TTL,PG
  No add_retention_policy or drop_chunks in release-3.6 schema.
  Row DELETE creates dead tuples and latest rows are not removed.
end note

== Backlog risk ==
Queue -> Node : sustained telemetry faster than database
Node -> HistoryQueue : queue.add continues
note over HistoryQueue
  LinkedBlockingQueue is unbounded.
  There is no DAO enqueue backpressure; monitor queueSize and heap.
end note
@enduml
